  "actor": "HARNESS",
  "what": "problem PD-1@v1 drafted",
  "phase": "DISCOVER",
  "minute": 55.0,
  "event_seq": 100,
  "root_problem": "Dispute tickets have roughly doubled since August (E-05), and 59% of those disputed bills (1785/3025) carry an ACTUAL, not ESTIMATED, read type (E-01) — meaning the surge is driven primarily by a billing-side defect that mis-processes bills even when a valid meter read exists, not by read-delivery/estimate-substitution failures or slow ticket handling (E-04 shows response times are within SLA). The best-supported candidate mechanism for this is a change to the billing import validation rules (DA-RULES) around the surge window (H-BILLING-RULE-CHANGE), which is consistent with E-01 but not yet directly confirmed via the billing-config rule-change log."
 },
